{"step_index":97,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-15T07:46:10Z","thinking":"The database file shows no data; it is either missing or empty. The correct Django database appears to be a different SQLite file. The absence of book entries suggests either manual upload without database updates or a missing migration. A script can populate the database with existing book data.\n\n\nThe chatbot UI failed to send messages because of a function rename. The test file uses an obsolete import that causes a crash. The requirements file is missing critical project dependencies. An outdated script runs a legacy Flask application instead of the intended Django project.\n\n\nThe project setup script needs to be updated to handle several missing steps. It must run migrations, create an admin user if one doesn't exist, and synchronize sample books before starting the Django development server on the correct port. The model lacks an `audio_file` field and corresponding handling in the serializer. There's no UI or API endpoints for administrators to upload and manage audio books, or to play them with a proper audio player. The permissions must be enforced such that only admins can delete, add, or modify books and audio files; regular users should only have read access.\n\n\nThe database lacks an admin user; this prevents testing of admin features. An admin account must be created with clear credentials provided in the project documentation. The current frontend is basic, so development should focus on creating a stunning modern UI. The new UI will incorporate a top navigation bar, welcome banner, search/filter bar, and sleek book cards, with aesthetics to include Glassmorphism, Cyber-Dark / Neomorphic styles, and smooth animations.\n\n\nThe book card design will integrate badges for content type (PDF, text, audio). Quick action buttons will provide read/view, listen (with audio player or text-to-speech fallback), and upload/delete (admin-only) functionality. An admin management panel will offer features to add books (including audio and PDF uploads), batch upload ZIP archives, and direct PDF upload and auto extraction.\n\n\nModern chatbot UI will incorporate a floating button with pulse animation, a glass chat window with smooth scroll and quick suggestion chips, typing indicators, and markdown/line break formatting. The chatbot will connect to Gemini AI via a dedicated API endpoint. The login/register process will be streamlined using an integrated modal or tabbed toggle with an interactive SVG avatar or modern card. Toast notifications will replace browser alerts. This is a significant feature addition; the implementation plan requires user approval.\n\n\nThe `Book` model requires an `audio_file` field. A database migration must be created and applied to include this new field. The `BookViewSet` permissions, currently using `IsAdminOrReadOnly`, must be assessed to ensure it handles multipart data for admin book uploads, specifically considering how it handles `POST` requests.\n\n\nThe `BookViewSet` requires updating to handle file uploads. Adding `MultiPartParser`, `FormParser`, and `JSONParser` to `parser_classes` enables accepting file uploads via `POST` and `PATCH`. Explicitly defining an `upload_audio` action with these parsers for a specific book id provides a clean endpoint for audio uploads. The existing `destroy()` method in `BookViewSet` correctly handles book deletion permissions via `IsAdminOrReadOnly`, ensuring only admins can delete books. The next step is to examine the serializer to ensure it correctly handles the file fields.\n\n\nThe serializer currently uses `SerializerMethodField` for `audio_file`, which causes issues during object creation and update because DRF treats them as read-only. This means file uploads via `POST` or `PATCH` will be ignored by the serializer's `save()` method. The `file` and `audio_file` fields should be kept as model `FileField` instances instead. The `to_representation` method can then be customized to return the appropriate file URLs.\n\n\nThe serializer's `to_representation` method was updated to construct the correct URLs for both `file` and `audio_file` fields, ensuring proper handling for both read and write operations. The `AIChatView` in `core/views.py` now includes error handling for the Gemini AI client, providing a user-friendly message if the client is unavailable, and the frontend's `sendMessage()` and `sendChatMessage()` functions will be addressed.\n\n\n`core/tests.py` and `test_api.py` need tests for admin actions (book and audio file uploads, deletion) and regular user restrictions. A script or management command to index existing PDF books from the `media/books/` directory into the database is required. Also need to create a default admin user.\n\n`run_project.py` should run migrations, populate the database with default data and an admin user, and start the Django server. Dependencies in `requirements.txt` must be updated to include Django, Django REST framework, simple JWT, CORS headers, Google GenAI, python-dotenv, and PyMuPDF.\n\n\nThe frontend design outlines a modern, feature-rich interface incorporating a glass navbar with search, category filters, and user/admin controls. A hero section will display dynamic statistics. The library grid will display book cards with cover mockups, genre indicators, and audio availability badges, alongside read and listen buttons that dynamically adapt to audio file presence.\n\n\nThe UI design requires several new components: admin-only book management modals for both adding books and uploading audio. An audio player bar with standard controls and an interactive seek bar must be implemented. Also planned is an AI librarian assistant widget that offers quick prompt suggestions and chat history. A combined auth modal or view is needed for login and registration.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan for fixing all codebase issues, adding audio book support to models and APIs, enforcing strict admin-only permissions for deleting and adding books/audiobooks, and building a modern frontend for SmartLibrary.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Implementation Plan - Modern Library Frontend, Audio Book Support & Permission Fixes\n\nFix all issues in the Aqlli Kutubxona codebase, implement comprehensive audio book support for books, restrict book deletion and addition (books & audiobooks) exclusively to admins, and deliver a modern, high-performance responsive frontend.\n\n---\n\n## User Review Required\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Key Architectural & Permission Rules**:\n> 1. **Only Admins** can delete books (`DELETE /api/books/<id>/`).\n> 2. **Only Admins** can add books and upload/attach audio books (`POST /api/books/`, `POST /api/books/<id>/upload-audio/`, `POST /api/upload-pdf/`, `POST /api/upload-zip/`).\n> 3. **Regular Users and Readers** can browse books, read PDFs, listen to audio books using the modern audio player, and chat with the AI librarian, but cannot delete or add books.\n> 4. We will add an `audio_file` field to the `Book` model and provide a seamless bottom audio player bar with play/pause, seekbar, speed control (1x, 1.25x, 1.5x, 2x), and time formatting.\n> 5. We will ensure default credentials exist for easy testing:\n>    - **Admin**: `admin@library.com` / `admin123`\n>    - **User**: `user@library.com` / `user123`\n> 6. We will populate existing 46 PDF books from `media/books/` into the database so the library is immediately rich with real content.\n\n---\n\n## Code Issues Identified & Solutions\n\n1. **`test_gemini.py` Crash during Django Test Discovery**:\n   - *Problem*: `test_gemini.py` imports deprecated `google.generativeai` which crashes on Python 3.14 with `TypeError: Metaclasses with custom tp_new are not supported.`.\n   - *Fix*: Update `test_gemini.py` to use modern `from google import genai` (`google-genai` library), matching `core/views.py`.\n2. **AI Chatbot Broken in Frontend**:\n   - *Problem*: `core/templates/core/index.html` calls `sendMessage()`, but the function was named `sendChatMessage()`, causing an unhandled JS ReferenceError when submitting chat messages.\n   - *Fix*: Fix function name and integrate smooth message streaming/bubbles and quick prompt chips.\n3. **Outdated `requirements.txt`**:\n   - *Problem*: `requirements.txt` only listed Flask dependencies and lacked Django, Django REST Framework, SimpleJWT, django-cors-headers, and google-genai.\n   - *Fix*: Update `requirements.txt` with complete, modern dependencies.\n4. **Outdated `run_project.py`**:\n   - *Problem*: `run_project.py` attempted to launch the legacy Flask `app.py` on `library.db` instead of the Django REST application.\n   - *Fix*: Update `run_project.py` to run Django migrations, ensure seed admin/user and books exist, and start `python manage.py runserver`.\n5. **No Audio Book Support in Backend**:\n   - *Problem*: `Book` model had no `audio_file` field. No serializer or API endpoints existed to handle audio files.\n   - *Fix*: Add `audio_file = models.FileField(upload_to='audio/', null=True, blank=True)` to `Book`, update `BookSerializer` to handle file URLs and audio uploads, and add `@action(detail=True, methods=['post'])` endpoint `upload_audio` on `BookViewSet`.\n6. **Admin-Only Permissions for Book & Audio Addition and Deletion**:\n   - *Problem*: Need strict verification that only admin (`is_staff` or `is_superuser`) can delete books or add/modify books and audio books.\n   - *Fix*: Enforce permissions in `BookViewSet` (`IsAdminOrReadOnly`), PDF/ZIP upload views, and the new audio upload view.\n7. **Empty Database**:\n   - *Problem*: 46 PDF books exist in `media/books/`, but `db.sqlite3` had 0 books and 0 admin users.\n   - *Fix*: Create a management command `populate_books` to seed books and ensure the admin user is created.\n\n---\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### Backend & Database Layer\n\n#### [MODIFY] [core/models.py](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/core/models.py)\n- Add `audio_file = models.FileField(upload_to='audio/', null=True, blank=True, verbose_name=\"Audio kitob fayli\")` to `Book` model.\n- Add `has_audio` helper property.\n\n#### [NEW] [core/migrations/0002_book_audio_file.py](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/core/migrations/0002_book_audio_file.py)\n- Migration generated via `makemigrations` to add `audio_file` to `Book`.\n\n#### [MODIFY] [core/serializers.py](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/core/serializers.py)\n- Include `audio_file` in `BookSerializer.Meta.fields`.\n- Handle absolute URL resolution for `audio_file` in `to_representation`.\n- Add `AudioUploadSerializer` for validating audio file uploads (`.mp3`, `.wav`, `.m4a`, `.ogg`, `.aac`).\n\n#### [MODIFY] [core/views.py](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/core/views.py)\n- In `BookViewSet`:\n  - Add `parser_classes = (MultiPartParser, FormParser, JSONParser)`.\n  - Add `@action(detail=True, methods=['post'], permission_classes=[IsAdminUser], parser_classes=[MultiPartParser, FormParser])` for `upload_audio`.\n  - Ensure delete and create operations strictly require admin privileges.\n- In `AIChatView`:\n  - Enhance fallback responses and error resilience.\n\n#### [NEW] [core/management/commands/setup_library.py](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/core/management/commands/setup_library.py)\n- Seed default admin user (`admin@library.com` / `admin123`) and test user (`user@library.com` / `user123`).\n- Scan `media/books/` and automatically register all existing PDF books in `db.sqlite3` with titles and descriptions.\n\n---\n\n### Modern Frontend Experience\n\n#### [MODIFY] [core/templates/core/index.html](file:///C:/Users/Surface%20PC/.gemini/core/templates/core/index.html)\nRedesign and upgrade the interface with:\n1. **Modern Aesthetic**:\n   - Deep cyber-glass dark theme with violet & teal glowing accents.\n   - Fluid typography and responsive layout.\n2. **Top Navigation & Controls**:\n   - Brand logo, live search bar (instant filter by title, author, genre).\n   - Category filter pills (Barchasi, Badiiy, Psixologiya, Roman, Diniy, Tarixiy, etc.).\n   - User profile badge with clear role indicator (`Admin` badge with crown vs `Kitobxon` badge).\n   - Admin action toolbar: \"Yangi Kitob Qo'shish\" button, PDF upload, ZIP upload.\n   - Clean logout & login/register toggles.\n3. **Hero Dashboard Stats**:\n   - Total Books count, Audio Books count, Categories count, AI status.\n4. **Enhanced Book Cards**:\n   - Stylized book card with genre badge, title, author, description preview.\n   - Status indicators: `[PDF]` and `[🎧 Audio]` badge if an audio book is attached.\n   - Action buttons:\n     - 📖 **O'qish (Read)**: Opens reader modal with PDF frame & extracted text.\n     - 🎧 **Tinglash (Listen)**:\n       - If `audio_file` exists: launches the floating audio player bar and starts playing the actual audio book.\n       - If no `audio_file`: uses browser text-to-speech with clear notice.\n     - 🎵 **Audio biriktirish (Add Audio Book)**: **Admin only**. Allows uploading an audio file specifically for this book.\n     - 🗑️ **O'chirish (Delete)**: **Admin only**. Prompts confirmation dialog and deletes book via API.\n5. **Modern Persistent Audio Player**:\n   - Floating bottom player bar with Play/Pause, 10s Skip/Back, interactive seekbar, elapsed/total time, volume slider, playback rate switcher (0.75x, 1x, 1.25x, 1.5x, 2x), and dismiss button.\n6. **Admin Modals**:\n   - **\"Yangi Kitob Qo'shish\" Modal**: Form with Title, Author, Genre, Description, PDF file input, and Audio Book file input.\n   - **\"Audio Kitob Yuklash\" Modal**: Quick audio upload for an existing book.\n7. **AI Librarian Chat Widget**:\n   - Fix `sendMessage` function.\n   - Quick prompt suggestion chips.\n   - Auto-scrolling chat history with formatting.\n8. **Toast Alert System**:\n   - Non-blocking notification toasts (Success, Error, Info) replacing browser alerts.\n\n---\n\n### Scripts & 